-- Practice data for SEAITT Legazpi LMS: fills the tables so every page has something to show.
--
-- It is only INSERT and UPDATE lines: no variables, no temporary tables, nothing to type. The people are the sample accounts of seaittlms_sample_accounts.sql,
-- so run the three files in this order, on a fresh database:
--   1. seaittlms_reset_and_rebuild.sql
--   2. seaittlms_sample_accounts.sql
--   3. this file   (File > Open SQL Script..., then press the lightning bolt; it can take a minute or two)
--
-- What it adds: the enrollment of the 40 students in 10 sections of the eight strands (grade 11 and grade 12, ACAD and TECH-PRO) in the 2nd term of 2026-2027, the courses
-- of the 12 teachers with their handouts, activities, quizzes and task performances, the library of the academic provider, the work handed in and its scores, who opened
-- what, the attendance of the last four weeks (Monday to Friday only), referrals, announcements, messages, notifications, friends, groups, files, the calendar, the security log, the system
-- settings and one teacher evaluation, and a quiz with every kind of question (with pictures): at least one row in every table.
--
-- The times are written from the moment you run it (for example, 3 days ago, or 5 days from now), so the work is due before and after today.
-- It is safe to run again: a row that is already there is skipped (INSERT IGNORE), nothing is added twice (a second run shows warnings, "Duplicate entry": that is the skipping).
-- Names, scores and answers are made up.

USE seaittlms;

SET NAMES utf8mb4;
SET FOREIGN_KEY_CHECKS = 0;

-- custom_roles: 2 new

